{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "mappingId": "pokemon_home_android",
  "platform": "mobile",
  "gameFamily": "pokemon_home",
  "coverage": "home-android-path-naming-and-unity-bundle-map",
  "notes": [
    "Pokémon HOME mobile models use predictable filename IDs. Community ripping docs (VG Resource, Xentax/barncastle) and the PogoEevee/PokemonHOMEBundles repo agree on pm####_##_## for species/form.",
    "Readable decrypted prefabs are often named pm0001_00_00_prefab.unity3d. Cloud bundles live under Models/Android/<Mitake*>/pokemons/pm####_##_##.",
    "On-device cache downloads land in Android/data/jp.pokemon.pokemonhome/files/tyranitar/ as cap####_f##_s#_128[_r].aba (encrypted) or mt_pv_ev_####_##_##.aba (Mitake preview/evolution).",
    "cap#### uses the National Dex number (cap0001 = Bulbasaur). f## is a form/skin id; s# is a shader/quality tier.",
    "Dependencies (rig, materials, extra textures) usually sit beside pokemons under Models/Android/**/dependencies/pm####_##_##.",
    "Encrypted .aba/.abap packages are detected and labeled but not decrypted by RAE."
  ],
  "games": [
    {
      "title": "Pokémon HOME Android",
      "shortTitle": "HOME",
      "packageIds": ["jp.pokemon.pokemonhome"]
    }
  ],
